## Plankton images and the imbalanced problem


```{r read_data}
isiis <- readRDS(here::here("data-raw", "isiis", "isiis.rds"))
isiis_taxa <- readRDS(here::here("data-raw", "isiis", "isiis_taxa.rds"))
```

```{r class_counts}
class_counts <- isiis |>
  count(truth, sort = TRUE) |>
  mutate(prop = n / sum(n)) |>
  left_join(isiis_taxa, by = join_by(truth == class))
print(class_counts, n = Inf)

non_plankton <- isiis_taxa |>
  filter(!plankton) |>
  pull(class)
```

The test set holds `r format(nrow(isiis), big.mark = " ")` objects in `r nlevels(isiis$truth)`
classes. Detritus alone accounts for
`r round(100 * class_counts$prop[class_counts$truth == "detritus"])`% of them.
`r length(non_plankton)` classes are not plankton:
`r paste(non_plankton, collapse = ", ")`.


